[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) says one bug: the parser reads dates month first. The <CauseCount ticket={4471} /> reports
merged into it describe <CauseCount ticket={4471} of="problems" /> different problems. Each got its own ticket, and
fixing one did not fix the other. Engineering closed #4471 on 5 October.

<Callout>
<code>parser</code>: fixed (fix(dates): parse dd/mm for eu locales). <code>hint</code>: won't fix, the booking-v3 form is retired.
Both tickets are closed.
</Callout>

## What #4471 holds

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

The table is the desk's own view, as exported: every report counted once, under the cause its tenant and channel
give it. The counts are computed when the page renders, so they follow the data as the desk keeps merging.

## The two problems

**`parser`: dates parse month first.** <CauseCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" /> reports from <CauseCount ticket={4471} problem="parser" of="tenants" />
tenants. Every tenant on file writes the day first, so any date with a day of 12 or less comes out swapped:
7 April becomes 4 July. This is the bug #4471 names. **Fixed**: the parser now reads dd/mm for EU locales.
[Issue 1](https://github.com/lmilewicz/mega-what-it-shows/issues/1), closed.

**`hint`: the booking form tells people to type month first.** <CauseCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" /> reports,
all through the form on the <CauseCount ticket={4471} problem="hint" of="tenants" /> booking-v3 tenants. The form
prints `MM/DD/YYYY`, people follow it, and the form reads their date day first. The symptom looks like the
parser bug, and the parser fix did not touch it. **Won't fix**: the booking-v3 form is retired, so no new reports
can come in this way. [Issue 2](https://github.com/lmilewicz/mega-what-it-shows/issues/2), closed.

The desk read <CauseCount ticket={4471} problem="moved" /> of the reports as a one-day move rather than a swap
(the footnote under the table). They come from day-first tenants outside the booking form, so they are filed under
`parser` and counted there, not as a third problem.

## Why they were merged

The desk merges on subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)), and both problems
arrive with the same subjects: "Date is wrong", "Wrong day on the invite". Intake tags did not help either: the tag
is a guess from the reporter's browser, and it disagrees with the tenant's form on dozens of the reports in the
table above. The cause comes from the tenant and the way the report came in: `src/lib/kb/causes.ts`.

## How the counts were checked

- The export has more rows than reports: its pages overlap, so the same report can appear twice. One id, one report.
- `npm run counts` runs the same `causes.ts` this page runs and prints the reports per cause.

